Package: ginteff
Type: Package
Title: Two- and Three-Way Interaction Effects (R Port of Stata's ginteff)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jesper", "Wulff", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "jwulff@econ.au.dk"),
    person("Marius", "Radean", role = "aut",
           comment = "Author of the original Stata 'ginteff' command (Stata Journal 23(2), 2023)"))
Description: Computes two- and three-way interaction effects -- via partial
    derivatives or first differences -- for fitted regression models, with
    delta-method standard errors. R port of the 'ginteff' Stata command
    (Radean, Stata Journal 23(2), 2023). Built as a thin wrapper around
    the 'marginaleffects' package: a 2^k counterfactual hypercube of
    interacted-variable vertices is built, average predictions per vertex
    are obtained from 'marginaleffects::avg_predictions()', and a signed
    linear combination is then formed manually using the per-vertex
    variance-covariance so that arbitrary 'vcov =' specifications (e.g.
    HC3, cluster, sandwich matrices) propagate through to the final
    interaction-effect standard error.
